 The weights between the input and reservoir, and between the reservoir and output layers, are trained. Reservoir nodes are typically sparsely connected and their weights are fixed, allowing the network to capture temporal dynamics through its internal state. Training focuses on the output weights only, making the learning process faster and more efficient compared to training all weights in a traditional recurrent neural network.","role":"assistant"},"model":"qwen2.5:7b","prompt_eval_count":773,"prompt_eval_duration":45262000,"total_duration":1645276800}}